Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.22,0:00:06.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.36,0:00:10.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is Resembool?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.21,0:00:12.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's awfully...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.57,0:00:15.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry it's too rural for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.51,0:00:19.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's still looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.85,0:00:21.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.73,0:00:25.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's been looking at me \Never since we were on the train.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.68,0:00:27.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can understand why, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.21,0:00:30.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a crime to be so beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.55,0:00:33.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.84,0:00:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're Sara, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.64,0:00:37.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure have grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.81,0:00:39.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, I'm not!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.57,0:00:51.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud, pretending to be someone he knows! That's the oldest...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.61,0:00:55.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sara...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.75,0:00:58.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was my mom's name...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.23,0:01:07.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this? You said you were going to study in Rush Valley,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.78,0:01:10.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but you've been in Central this whole time?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.30,0:01:14.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not like that. We've been keeping an eye on Ed and Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.31,0:01:15.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.32,0:01:19.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, when are those two coming back?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.73,0:01:24.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, Grandma, I met someone in Rush Valley who said they knew you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.38,0:01:30.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma, no one's home! \NNo one, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.86,0:01:32.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good grief...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.09,0:01:35.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.96,0:01:44.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, the power of love!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.91,0:01:46.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've come back, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.96,0:01:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pinako-san, I can't seem to locate my house.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.41,0:01:54.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your house, as such, is no longer...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.18,0:01:56.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma, you know this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.71,0:01:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, right. You were still \Nso little, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.56,0:02:03.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This man is Ed and Al's father.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.66,0:02:09.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and coming back \Nafter being away for so long,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.28,0:02:11.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't seem to find my house.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.46,0:02:15.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.55,0:02:21.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.13,0:02:25.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.08,0:02:29.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.49,0:04:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How come you're so fast?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.39,0:04:29.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? My body just seems \Nawfully light for some reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.98,0:04:32.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're tired, \Nshould we take a break?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.94,0:04:38.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.29,0:04:41.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you said before \Nwas probably the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.66,0:04:44.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About Führer Bradley?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.34,0:04:48.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That man... the Führer...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.94,0:04:50.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is a homunculus!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.75,0:04:55.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, the Führer was \Ncommanding the mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.23,0:04:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think it was Envy \Ntaking his place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.18,0:05:02.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, the Führer's secretary was a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.30,0:05:04.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we go back to the military, you and I both would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.66,0:05:07.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, Brother, sure enough, that secretary lady is—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.23,0:05:08.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.34,0:05:12.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Sensei said that homunculi are made when a human transmutation fails.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.15,0:05:14.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you not to say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.73,0:05:28.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.62,0:05:31.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that just now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.53,0:05:35.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A huge gate... \NI've seen it before, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.14,0:05:38.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, was that truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.55,0:05:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei said it was \Nsomething else, but yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.92,0:05:45.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How did that happen, \Nwhen all we did is touch?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.87,0:05:51.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As an alchemist, I must have unknowingly made the Philosopher's Stone react.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.50,0:05:53.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, do you believe it, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.16,0:05:55.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That I've become \Na Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.20,0:06:02.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't feel like that's \Nwhat happened myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.69,0:06:05.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, the Philosopher's Stone \Nwouldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.22,0:06:06.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody has ever seen one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.99,0:06:09.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whatever form it takes, it wouldn't surprise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.48,0:06:11.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But never mind that. \NDon't get too close to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.78,0:06:14.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.02,0:06:17.76,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If we inadvertently touch again, it will spark another reaction with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.76,0:06:22.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no sense in having you disappear before we can take your body back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.07,0:06:28.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.12,0:06:29.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Resembool.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.49,0:06:31.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where the military will look first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.80,0:06:35.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those homunculi are \Nsure to come after you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.43,0:06:37.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to beat them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.59,0:06:39.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's something \Nthat we have to get.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.17,0:07:01.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly was apparently confirmed dead \Nin front of that red light.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.38,0:07:04.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, at that moment, Scar was still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.55,0:07:10.32,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It appears that the townspeople fled outside the city before the military rushed in.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.68,0:07:14.76,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We've discovered an underground passage, and we're tracing where it leads now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.76,0:07:18.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean they \Nweren't trying to resist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.88,0:07:20.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was their objective
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.41,0:07:23.58,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,to use the military as ingredients, \Nmaking the whole city a transmutation circle?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.58,0:07:25.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed and Al appear to be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.78,0:07:29.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Several soldiers witnessed Ed outside the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.06,0:07:35.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They said that about an hour ago, Ed and Al were leaving the area.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.01,0:07:38.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could they be continuing \Non their journey? Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.04,0:07:42.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt that they were helping Scar to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.80,0:07:43.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.24,0:07:52.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,28 dead, 67 seriously injured, including five officers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.82,0:07:55.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are still over 900 others missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.82,0:07:59.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will conduct a thorough \Ninvestigation as to what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.39,0:08:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is one person who \Nknows exactly what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.12,0:08:05.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.60,0:08:07.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.57,0:08:09.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Elric brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.53,0:08:13.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For what reason \Ndid they show up in Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.67,0:08:16.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We believe that \Nthey were pursuing Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.01,0:08:19.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why? Did he have orders \Nto subdue Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.94,0:08:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, they were engaged in various \Nfields of inquiry and alchemic research.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.44,0:08:28.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They appeared in Liore \Nand had dealings with Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.82,0:08:33.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have as many as a thousand officers \Nand men become casualties as a result?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.94,0:08:37.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though he has a rope \Naround the Elric brothers' necks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.34,0:08:41.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would like to give them \Na chance to explain themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.53,0:08:46.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying you will \Napprehend them yourself? Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.62,0:08:51.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if you fail to catch them, {\i1}you{\i0} will be the one who will have to explain himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.48,0:08:53.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.75,0:09:01.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to my intelligence,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.02,0:09:08.14,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,the Elric brothers might be fighting alongside a seditious element that calls themselves homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.14,0:09:09.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catch him and bring him back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.66,0:09:11.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it gets out of hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.16,0:09:13.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I grant you permission to pass judgment on him on the spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.26,0:09:19.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.62,0:09:20.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You heard what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.92,0:09:23.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sort through all the information we have \Non sightings of the Elric brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.11,0:09:27.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we really going to \Ngo after Ed and Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.91,0:09:29.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are our orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.42,0:09:32.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But this was the work of Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.56,0:09:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's also partially Archer's fault \Nfor being reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.61,0:09:37.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what went down here, \Nbut the brothers—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.18,0:09:38.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fact is, they've run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.92,0:09:41.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we let them go, it's going to come down on the Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.18,0:09:43.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said that if things get out of hand, \Nthe Colonel was to kill them!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.80,0:09:47.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we get going, Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.40,0:09:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.02,0:10:39.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you stay here again \Nall last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.96,0:10:40.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.78,0:10:46.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just don't have a good grasp on my sense of the passage of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.35,0:10:49.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How many years has it been \Nsince Trisha died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.11,0:10:51.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been six years now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.50,0:10:55.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. The children \Nmust have grieved, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.84,0:11:00.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sara Rockbell?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.17,0:11:02.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I thought you were Sara.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.32,0:11:04.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you before, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.28,0:11:08.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Winry. \NSara was my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.57,0:11:17.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's how.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.42,0:11:19.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The war, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.44,0:11:23.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't just war. \NThey were killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.22,0:11:25.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And by a soldier who would ordinarily be their ally.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.96,0:11:29.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All because they treated \Nfriends and foes impartially.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.14,0:11:31.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.36,0:11:34.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't make it \Nsound so simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.31,0:11:36.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not just sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.40,0:11:38.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.37,0:11:40.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,know the man who \Nkilled my parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.69,0:11:43.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I also know that he is \Nby no means a bad person.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.28,0:11:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So I can't even do \Nanything about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.98,0:11:49.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.81,0:11:53.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why it's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.12,0:12:17.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-san! I'm so hungry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.05,0:12:21.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,L-Lieutenant Ross!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.68,0:12:22.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Brosh!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.57,0:12:26.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really have come after us, haven't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.59,0:12:29.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because we saw something we weren't supposed to see!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.77,0:12:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, sure enough, \Nyou've come after us!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.82,0:12:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.15,0:12:48.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.10,0:12:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys don't even have a home anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.68,0:12:55.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you mean, those two are being pursued by the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.90,0:12:59.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We got an emergency phone call, \Nfrom the east.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.25,0:13:04.00,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,They said that by the Führer's order, we were to apprehend the Fullmetal Alchemist and his brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.00,0:13:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that they'd been in contact with the masterminds behind the revolt in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.20,0:13:10.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are those guys doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.18,0:13:14.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone I'm close to in \NCommunications told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.70,0:13:18.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Currently, a search party is being \Ndrawn up by Major General Hakuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.81,0:13:21.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Word has probably already gone out to local police.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.27,0:13:25.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once that happened, the Lieutenant suddenly took some leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.59,0:13:27.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought \Nthis would be a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.71,0:13:30.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nice to be able to \Nbreathe the clean air, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.43,0:13:33.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can you go to all this trouble \Njust to tell all this to a wanted man?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.03,0:13:35.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.32,0:13:38.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if the Führer {\i1}did{\i0} order it, \NI don't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.69,0:13:40.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could those two be rebels?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.53,0:13:41.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, I didn't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.64,0:13:45.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, we don't know whether or not \Nthe two of them are even coming here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.61,0:13:48.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, they'll come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.90,0:13:52.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even without a house to return to, \Nthis is still their home, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.19,0:13:55.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, you're here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.92,0:13:59.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Long ago, there weren't \Nany railroads into here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.16,0:14:05.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There wasn't even a single road that went further east, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.78,0:14:10.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone used to climb the mountain alongside that stream
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.30,0:14:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,until it finally let out in the east.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.63,0:14:16.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We used to play a lot \Nby that stream, long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.44,0:14:19.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it! If I were Ed and Al, \NI would definitely come that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.84,0:14:21.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Uncle!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.38,0:14:23.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Un...cle?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.36,0:14:23.50,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Scieszka!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.50,0:14:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ross-san, you guys stay here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.45,0:14:28.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the search party shows up, \Nwe'll slow them down as best we can!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.49,0:14:29.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.09,0:14:34.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There weren't any \Nrailroads into here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.50,0:14:37.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that was over \Na hundred years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.10,0:14:48.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, hide!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.07,0:14:53.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.78,0:14:55.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just take cover!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.60,0:15:02.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So ultimately, this is all \Njust about some promotion?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.43,0:15:05.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say that's the only reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.59,0:15:07.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said so, didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.06,0:15:09.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the Elric brothers get away,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.02,0:15:12.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel will bear full responsibility for what happened in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.45,0:15:14.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel will?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.18,0:15:16.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, there isn't much we can do, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.68,0:15:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hey there, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.86,0:15:26.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just as the Colonel predicted.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.78,0:15:29.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're taking the side road to your hometown that you're used to taking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.14,0:15:35.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.23,0:15:36.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.72,0:15:37.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.35,0:15:40.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm never going back to the military!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.74,0:15:45.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go ahead and fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.16,0:15:48.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See whether or not you can \Nshoot through my Automail!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.43,0:15:50.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,E-Edward-kun, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.34,0:15:51.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go ahead and shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.80,0:15:52.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.16,0:16:02.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.06,0:16:08.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.52,0:16:10.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.80,0:16:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.66,0:16:16.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come quietly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.33,0:16:23.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.04,0:16:25.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've got something to say, \Nwe're all ears!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.75,0:16:27.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't your enemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.82,0:16:31.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can prove your innocence as much as you want to during the formal inquiry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.39,0:16:34.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be okay for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.99,0:16:39.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do those two seriously \Nmean to turn against us?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.07,0:16:41.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find out \Nwhen we catch them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.49,0:16:44.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody get cold feet next time!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.90,0:16:49.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, um, could you \Nget into my breast pocket?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.09,0:16:56.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take better care of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.25,0:17:00.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't have gotten very far.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.58,0:17:03.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Probably because they can't very well \Nexpose Alphonse to the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.77,0:17:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because of his bloodseal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.31,0:17:22.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Out of the way!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.14,0:17:40.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who was it that told you about the Elric brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.94,0:17:42.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.83,0:17:47.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you seriously think that those two are rebels?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.05,0:17:49.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll know once we catch them \Nand interrogate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.88,0:17:55.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're{\i0} the one who recruited Ed and Al, aren't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.88,0:17:56.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.74,0:17:58.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.72,0:18:02.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The only thing this man is interested in \Nis his rank within the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.01,0:18:03.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.22,0:18:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was this how it was when you killed my father and mother, too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.59,0:18:21.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.70,0:18:25.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't touch me carelessly! \NWe don't know what will happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.04,0:18:50.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you running?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.08,0:18:53.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.61,0:18:55.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.11,0:18:58.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you're chasing us, that's why.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.73,0:19:01.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When a dog is chased, he runs away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.95,0:19:05.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A well-trained dog never \Ngoes against his master's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.63,0:19:06.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you say "master"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.75,0:19:10.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or, have you suddenly \Ngone back to being a stray dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.93,0:19:12.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Relax, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.91,0:19:14.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you were cursed as a dog of the military,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.37,0:19:15.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you would put up with it \Nin order to achieve your goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.88,0:19:17.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that what you said?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.63,0:19:23.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm through being \Na dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.17,0:19:27.47,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Does this mean you're going back to being \Na helpless child who won't listen to reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.47,0:19:29.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Call it whatever you want!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.29,0:19:37.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're slipping, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.80,0:19:38.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.83,0:19:40.68,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.40,0:19:59.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.41,0:20:04.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I transmuted the stone projectile in mid-air...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.20,0:20:07.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...and I compressed the air within it and ignited it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.68,0:20:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An effective attack, was it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.77,0:20:12.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That must have come in handy \Nin Ishbal, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.41,0:20:29.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.01,0:20:48.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,620)}Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.92,0:20:57.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please... stop...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.84,0:20:58.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.11,0:21:04.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once, I killed two people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.71,0:21:08.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were doctors.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.79,0:21:12.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were no friends or foes \Namong their patients.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.48,0:21:15.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what they said as they treated those around the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.75,0:21:19.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, those whom they treated became our enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.57,0:21:23.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military repeatedly asked them \Nto stop treating our enemies,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.27,0:21:24.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but they refused to listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.92,0:21:30.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was given an order... \Nand I... shot them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.42,0:21:38.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ever since, I swore that \Neven if I were under orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.81,0:21:41.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would not follow anything that was unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.29,0:21:45.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That I would put myself in a position where I didn't have to follow them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.15,0:21:50.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason I'm chasing after you is not because I was ordered to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.94,0:21:53.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because I'm pissed off at you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.69,0:21:58.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you run off on your own \Nwithout coming to me for protection?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.64,0:23:40.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.45,0:23:44.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 44: "Hohenheim of Light"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.28,0:23:47.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the hell are you doing here...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.43,0:23:50.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you rotten old man?!
